# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Afrizone web-portal: production build-time env vars for Cloudflare Pages
# Set these in Pages → afrizone-portal → Settings → Environment variables
# (Production environment). Vite bakes them into the build, so a change
# requires a rebuild/redeploy, not just a server restart.
#
# This is the STORE and COURIER facing app, deployed at
# portal.parttime.afrizonemart.com. The staff console is a separate Pages
# project (afrizone → admin.parttime.afrizonemart.com) and a separate audience;
# do not point one at the other's environment variables.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# REQUIRED. The deployed API's origin (no trailing slash, no /api suffix).
#
# Never api.afrizonemart.com - that is Afrizoma's separate e-commerce backend,
# and pointing this at it would send store owners' credentials to a system that
# has never heard of them.
#
# The API must also list this app's origin in CORS_ORIGIN (server/wrangler.jsonc)
# or every request from here is refused by the browser before it arrives. That is
# a deploy-time pairing: changing one without the other breaks the portal in a
# way the API's own logs will not show.
VITE_API_URL=https://api.parttime.afrizonemart.com
